139534649 true] [17592186301373 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534649 true] [17592186301373 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\n- $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\n- $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301373 1113 #uuid "c87fb501-fa8f-570c-af52-809859c824eb" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301373 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301375 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301376 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301377 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301378 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301379 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1041 "selection" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301375 13194139534649 true] [17592186301374 1110 #uuid "7c301dfb-b9c0-53fd-a0c9-f0adb0313e2a" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301375 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301375 1111 #uuid "884a8bc6-2153-5324-9674-77d113cabe80" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301376 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301376 1111 #uuid "c4f76996-b987-5b4c-be48-8fa8d25a2d0d" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301377 1034 "III only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301377 1111 #uuid "1293b599-e383-521b-baf8-c2d67023339f" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301378 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301378 1111 #uuid "17bd9af2-5a00-506c-add5-bb1f361bd05a" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301379 1034 "II only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301379 1111 #uuid "ee780c7e-4fd0-5914-a6e6-ebcf46378d42" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301380 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301381 13194139534649 true] [17592186301380 1089 "q-117371" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301380 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534649 true] [17592186301380 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\n- $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n- $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3})$\n- $(0,0)$" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301380 1113 #uuid "3728d7d4-f4c7-5690-9736-e69533d0a6ab" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301380 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{7\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{7\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(0,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,0)$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301382 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301383 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301384 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301385 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301386 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1041 "selection" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301383 13194139534649 true] [17592186301381 1110 #uuid "d17a735b-b5cf-54cd-ae19-a117e3f945cb" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301382 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301382 1111 #uuid "9f061aef-c3cc-59a4-8be8-b6da5789c1d5" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301383 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301383 1111 #uuid "7eada3b6-cb43-5f7e-8ab1-ee3bdd42cc2e" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301384 1034 "III only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301384 1111 #uuid "8a31bd1a-95d4-5553-a904-219978f22b39" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301385 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301385 1111 #uuid "6849c656-103c-5cbc-8ee3-3669895845cd" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301386 1034 "II only" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301386 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534649 true] [17592186301386 1111 #uuid "f8a0c2ef-0a50-5f07-b4a9-674ffff968ef" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301387 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301388 13194139534649 true] [17592186301387 1089 "q-66006" 13194139534649 true] [17592186301387 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534649 true] [1759